        TASK - Meet Lyren - Resistance Contact NPC:
            > ACQUIRED:
                (no acquired task):
            > COMPLETED:
                Lyren - (softly, eyes distant) The land... it aches. Not just the ground. The hearts walking upon it. I can feel every fracture like a wound that never closed.:
                Kaera - You speak as if the world itself is alive. As if it is suffering.:
                Lyren - It is. And it grows worse with every passing day. Seth believes the airship can carry us forward... but a machine alone cannot mend what is broken. We need anchors. Pieces of what once held meaning.:
                Moxie - Oooh, cryptic *and* poetic. I like her already.:
                Chock - Skip the poetry. What do you need?:
                Lyren - (small, gentle smile) A Fragrant Hibiscus... said to bloom only where hope once refused to die. And an Ancient Relic from the old ruin -- something that still remembers what the world was before the fractures.:
                Lyren - Bring them to me. They may help us stabilize the region long enough for Seth to prepare the Rustwing.:
                Poise - (nodding quietly) Symbols have power. We will find them.:
                Kade - Great. Treasure hunt for sentimental value. My favorite.:
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - lyren ("The land is breaking down faster than we can fix it. Help stabilize the region before Seth can prepare the airship for departure."):
                EVENT - dungeon_add_treasure - fragrant_hibiscus (seth_hideout_ch3 - final_chamber):
                EVENT - dungeon_add_treasure - ancient_relic (abandoned_ruin_ch2 - final_chamber):
                EVENT - award_task - deliver_fragrant_hibiscus_to_lyren

        TASK - Deliver Fragrant Hibiscus to Lyren - Item:
            > ACQUIRED:
                (no acquired task):
            > COMPLETED:
                Lyren - (taking the hibiscus carefully, closing her eyes as she breathes in its scent):
                Lyren - ...It's still alive. Even after everything... it kept its fragrance. Like a small act of defiance.:
                Lyren - (softly, almost to herself) These were the first flowers my mother planted after... I thought they'd all gone.:
                Kaera - (gently) Then this one still carries her hope.:
                Lyren - (nodding slowly) That's what I needed. Not just the flower itself...:
                Lyren - but proof that something can still remember what it was supposed to be. Even when the world tries to forget.:
                Moxie - (grinning) You really do turn everything into poetry, don't you?:
                Lyren - (looking at him with quiet intensity) Everything broken still holds its original shape somewhere inside.:
                Lyren - 6If we forget that... then the Fracture has already won.:
                EVENT - remove_item - fragrant_hibiscus:
